# oracle: fix srd on a triclinic box (examples/ASPHERE/line in.line.srd cut down to a 2d box of 16 x 16 A with two big spheres of diameter 2 and SRD particles at density 10): 10 steps orthogonal, then change_box all triclinic and fix deform xy erate 0.0002 remap v for 10 steps; the SRD bin temperature (f_2[9]) and the per-atom state
# engine vs native fixture: measured below
# native: installed lmp (b332f28)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      sphere
dimension       2
boundary        p p p
region          box block -8 8 -8 8 -0.5 0.5
create_box      2 box
lattice         sq 10.0
create_atoms    2 box
create_atoms    1 single -4 0 0 units box
create_atoms    1 single 3 2.5 0 units box
group           big type 1
group           small type 2
set             type 1 diameter 2.0
set             type 1 density 0.5
set             type 2 diameter 0.0
set             group small mass 0.01
pair_style      lj/cut 1.5
pair_coeff      * * 0.0 1.0
delete_atoms    overlap 1.0 small big
velocity        small create 1.44 87287 loop geom
neighbor        0.8 multi
comm_modify     vel yes
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check yes
timestep        0.0001
fix             1 big nve/sphere
fix             2 small srd 20 big 1.0 0.25 49894 search 0.2 cubic warn 0.0001 shift yes 49829 overlap yes collision noslip
fix             3 all enforce2d
compute         tsmall small temp
thermo          5
thermo_style    custom step c_tsmall f_2[9] atoms
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             10
change_box      all triclinic
fix             4 all deform 1 xy erate 0.0002 units box remap v
run             10
